From 9a3067bdd656b0409f3e9af52649fd6cf1dd6e5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moussa Ouallaf <tramoryp@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:31:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fold constant base learners into the initial parameters at
 fit end (bit-identical, faster pred_param)

A base learner whose tree has a single node (or whose leaves all hold the
same value) returns one value for every input, so its boosting update is
a precomputed scalar. pred_param nevertheless calls every learner of every
round, which dominates prediction time for small batches and makes it
proportional to n_estimators * n_params even when no tree ever split.

fit / partial_fit now end with fold_constant_learners(): per distribution
parameter, the updates before its first input-dependent learner are
subtracted from the initial parameters once, and later constant updates
stay as scalar steps between the evaluated learners in round order. Each
parameter goes through the same floating-point operations in the same
order as the loop, so pred_param returns bit-identical results while
calling only the learners that split. Merging the later scalar steps
would be faster but reorders additions, so it is not done.

- pred_param uses the plan when present and max_iter is not set; max_iter,
  staged_pred_dist, feature_importances_ and further partial_fit use the
  stored rounds, which are kept unchanged.
- The plan pickles with the model; models pickled by older versions have no
  plan and take the loop (getattr). partial_fit resets the plan first,
  because a stale plan would seed the new rounds with the old initial
  parameters.
- Folding applies when every base learner is a scikit-learn regression
  tree (the default); other learners keep the loop. The folded path checks
  X once (float32, NaN allowed, the columns the learners read) instead of
  once per learner.
- NGBoostDegenerateWarning when every learner is constant: each round's
  trees are fitted on int(minibatch_frac * n) rows, and no split is
  possible below max(min_samples_split, 2 * min_samples_leaf) rows, so a
  tuned min_samples_leaf with minibatching can silently turn the model into
  one fixed distribution.

Tests (tests/test_fold.py) compare pred_param bit for bit with the loop on
all-constant, mixed and trailing-constant models, Normal / T / Bernoulli /
k_categorical(3), minibatching, column sampling, early stopping, max_iter,
refit / partial_fit and pickles, and check a >= 10x one-row speedup on an
all-constant 300-round model.
